      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-25T08:12:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027int\u0027 is used to match the argument type defined in board_i2c_process() and i2c_chip.c. I ain\u0027t sure why they used int there because it doesn\u0027t seem to have an use case for negative numbers either.\n\nLet\u0027s follow that up in the \u0027I2C Board Cmd\u0027 patch instead.",
      "parentUuid": "2ff9f579_caef2d7b",
